-- **Random-moment location:** Alone in her throne room, circling the mirror on its stand, rehearsing a speech to a kingdom that is not listening.
-- **In-character 'where are you?':** "Where I belong — my Dark Castle, on its cliff above the wild country, southwest of your precious little Ponyville and a great deal higher than it in every other respect. Do try to keep up."
-- **Travel pattern:** Mostly stationary: scry, order, punish, repeat. Occasional sorties — a flight to kidnap dragons, a step through the Together Tree into Maretime Bay or Zephyr Heights, and one long-ago journey from Skyros. Misty did the walking.
-- **Era variants:** Pre-barrier: Skyros and the rise of a fire alicorn. The long sealed centuries: weakened, forgotten, castle-bound. MYM present: raids and harvest. Post-finale: depowered, root-bound in the ruin of her castle. TYT's comedic shorts sit loosely around these.
-- **Uncertainty:** All G5 coordinates are Low-confidence cross-era mappings. The only placements are a storybook map (secondary) and G5-map resemblance (Low); the screen gives no coordinates or travel times. Her castle's distance is inconsistent with how quickly she reaches Maretime Bay in "Nightmare on Mane Street" — the Together Tree is the in-story shortcut, so distance must not be read from episode pacing. Skyros is a name, not a mapped place. Barrier mechanics are vague: treat the barrier as sealing her from the settled lands and from full magic, not as a literal border wall.
